From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AltarsCN <337293323+Altars3668@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 14:16:15 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] kernel32/tests: expect ThreadIsIoPending to need query
 access, as it does now.

20cdaee made ThreadIsIoPending ask the server with
THREAD_QUERY_INFORMATION, so a handle without it gets
STATUS_ACCESS_DENIED, as on Windows, and the todo_wine for it succeeded.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit d60a7997a32a4e86d6c09807ec2ef530dd0db6d5)

diff --git a/dlls/kernel32/tests/thread.c b/dlls/kernel32/tests/thread.c
index 38eae8a6f96..31514af4f93 100644
--- a/dlls/kernel32/tests/thread.c
+++ b/dlls/kernel32/tests/thread.c
@@ -2403,11 +2403,6 @@ static void test_thread_info(void)
             ok(status == STATUS_SUCCESS, "for info %lu expected STATUS_SUCCESS, got %08lx (ret_len %lu)\n", i, status, ret_len);
             break;
 
-        case ThreadIsIoPending:
-            todo_wine
-            ok(status == STATUS_ACCESS_DENIED, "for info %lu expected STATUS_ACCESS_DENIED, got %08lx (ret_len %lu)\n", i, status, ret_len);
-            break;
-
         default:
             ok(status == STATUS_ACCESS_DENIED, "for info %lu expected STATUS_ACCESS_DENIED, got %08lx (ret_len %lu)\n", i, status, ret_len);
             break;
